===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:major<ety:der<la:maior>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|major|}}, from {{der|en|la|maior}}, comparative of {{m|la|magnus||great, large; noble, important}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*méǵh₂yōs||greater}}, comparative of {{m|ine-pro|*meǵh₂-||great}}. Compare {{cog|fy|majoar||major}}, {{cog|nl|majoor||major}}, {{cog|fr|majeur}}. {{doublet|en|mayor}}.

{{senseno|en|military rank|cap=1}} is a shortening of {{m|en|sergeant major}}, perhaps after {{der|en|es|mayor}} in the same sense.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|id=8319622990}}</ref>

